  "id": "Compound::DB00454 - Gene::1565",
  "verbalization": "Pethidine, as a member of the Full Opioid Agonists class, is linked to Cyp2d6 through a series of molecular interactions that involve both receptor activation and enzyme binding. The evidence suggests that Pethidine, along with its analogs like Dextropropoxyphene and Dihydrocodeine, binds to the opioid receptor, which is a key step in its pharmacological action. This receptor activation is supported by the lowest common ancestor (LCA) relationship between Pethidine and its analogs, which points to the Opioid Receptor Agonist as a shared functional node. The binding of these compounds to Cyp2d6, as indicated by the LCA relationship between Pethidine and Oxycodone, suggests a broader mechanism where opioid agonists may influence enzyme activity through indirect pathways. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for opioid receptor activation in modulating Cyp2d6 function, though the exact mechanism of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
